{
 "id": "threads/change-stays-on-its-thread",
 "description": "One session, three threads: main, p:side and a:sub. main reports a cmdfilter change and then applies it again, +$0.02625 as new and +$0.00210 when applied again. The side thread and the subagent send the same body and carry no change, so main's change is priced on neither: they have no op. Later each reports the same ChangeID in its own request. Each prices it as new (a write), and no unique_change failure is raised, because that check runs inside one request. The side thread then applies it again, as a read. Each thread keeps its own state, so main's change is never applied to another thread. (The Version lock of each thread is checked by TestThreadsOfOneSessionKeepTheirOwnChangesAndVersions, not by a case.)",
 "source": "issue_cases.md",
 "dims": {
  "kind": "rewrite",
  "position": "afterBStarToL",
